Issue 31 is done. Summary:

**1. Deflaked the resolver-rotation test.** Root cause (proven by reproduction under concurrent `bun test` processes): the `gitStubHarness` WAIT_MERGED poll ran `git log | grep -q` under `set -o pipefail`. When `grep -q` matched it closed the pipe, git log died on SIGPIPE (141), and pipefail reported the pipeline as failed despite the match — so ticket 02's "wait for the sibling's merge" could spuriously exit 42, killing the second merge-approval. Fixed by capturing git log into a shell variable and matching with `case`, which is pipe-free. Before: ~3-4 failures per 6 concurrent runs. After: 36 consecutive concurrent full-suite runs green. This was a test-stub bug, not an engine defect, confirming ticket 22's inference.

**2. UTF-8 head-boundary fix.** `readLogRange` now head-trims via a new `utf8HeadTrim` (drops a leading continuation byte) and reports `offset = start + headTrim`, so a tail-first open or load-earlier read that starts mid-character never decodes U+FFFD at the pane head. Regression test added beside the existing boundary tests.

**3. Detail width persistence pinned.** Moved parse-and-clamp of the stored `console-detail-width` string into a pure `parseStoredDetailWidth` in project.ts (used by view.ts), and pinned the round trip at the projection seam in project.test.ts.

**4. Em dashes.** None remain in `engine/*.ts`; ticket 29's colon reword holds.

All five acceptance criteria ticked in the Issue; state set to `done`; committed as `aec2f65` on `pool/31` (outcome JSON written).
